            <ArticleTitle>Intravascular stenting of the right internal mammary artery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>252-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Despite its tortuous course and small caliber, percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty of the internal mammary artery can be performed with a high initial success rate (82-94%). The successful deployment of a balloon expandable coil stent at the mid-right internal mammary artery in a patient with recurrent stenosis of that graft is reported.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
